WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:03.329
What assumptions do you make when you meet a Jewish person?

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:08.900
Are they based more on media, your parents, or just unreliable sources?

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:10.200
This is how I win.

00:00:11.889 --> 00:00:15.900
As you play along this episode of Odd Man Out, think of how you pick the mole.

00:00:19.719 --> 00:00:21.719
We brought together seven Jewish people.

00:00:21.719 --> 00:00:23.719
I'm Jewish.

00:00:23.719 --> 00:00:26.789
I am Jewish.

00:00:27.369 --> 00:00:29.369
One of them is a liar.

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:32.939
If the group discovers who the liar is, they'll split a cash prize.

00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:39.000
If the liar survives, they win the entire prize.

00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:42.700
Who is the Odd Man Out?

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:46.520
Alright so who's the mole? I'm just going to ask right away, well who is it? Come on, come on.

00:00:46.660 --> 00:00:50.580
Okay, where have all your families been expelled from? Can we just, like get into that like real quick?

00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:54.980
Every Jew has a story about being forcibly taken from their home.

00:00:54.980 --> 00:00:58.300
My family got expelled from Russia early 1900s moved to New York.

00:00:58.300 --> 00:00:59.500
Are you Ashkenazi?

00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:00.000
- Yeah.
- Okay

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:01.080
Versus?

00:01:01.700 --> 00:01:03.180
God I can never remember the other one-

00:01:03.180 --> 00:01:04.000
- Sephardic.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:05.580
Oh, really? Interesting.

00:01:05.980 --> 00:01:07.450
I actually converted.

00:01:07.450 --> 00:01:09.839
My mom is from the Philippines. My dad is from Mississippi.

00:01:09.869 --> 00:01:11.000
Why did you convert?

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:13.200
My mom put me into it when I was really young, when I was like six or seven so

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:16.100
I just always grew up with it. So, I didn't really feel like I converted.

00:01:16.100 --> 00:01:18.900
My family is Polish. I am half Jewish.

00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:22.439
So my mom through birth, I am Jewish. My dad is Christian.

00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:27.720
My safta (grandmother in Hebrew) was expelled from Turkey and my saba (grandfather) was from Bulgaria.

00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:29.600
Good words.

00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:30.400
Yeah.

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:32.300
I don't think everyone here knows Hebrew.

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:34.600
Does anyone else know Hebrew?

00:01:34.600 --> 00:01:35.300
Yeah.

00:01:35.300 --> 00:01:36.400
That means grandma and grandpa.

00:01:36.500 --> 00:01:37.600
Do you know fluently?

00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:38.400
Yeah.

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:39.680
My mom is Israeli so- Okay, yeah same.

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:43.400
Do you guys, um, like know all the holidays?

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:48.000
Everyone was drawing out questions and answers and it was just tough to get your- your piece in.

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:52.700
But I was definitely worried that I'll just be voted off just because I may not look Jewish.

00:01:52.700 --> 00:01:54.800
What's like the highest holiday?

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:55.300
Oh, that's a good word.

00:01:57.540 --> 00:01:58.900
Yom Kippur and Rosh Hashanah.

00:01:58.900 --> 00:02:01.000
If someone said Hanukkah, I was like "done!" "Out"

00:02:01.060 --> 00:02:02.200
Anyone go to Jewish school?

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:05.960
I went to Jewish preschool, elementary school and high school and learnt Hebrew in all of them.

00:02:05.960 --> 00:02:07.600
So, I'm very Jewish.

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:11.400
Can you start reciting like the first prayer of Hanukkah? Like the first word?

00:02:12.800 --> 00:02:14.900
I mean, I know it's not the first word. It just flows better this way.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:16.900
Yeah, that wasn't really the first word, but...

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:21.800
He said his prayer really fast and it didn't sound like a hundred percent to me.

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:26.400
What's the prayer just, like the two words for, like washing your hands before you eat?

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:27.500
No!

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:28.500
No, I don't know.

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:29.700
Netilat Yadayim.

00:02:30.100 --> 00:02:31.200
No, I got you. I tru-

00:02:32.200 --> 00:02:35.600
Quick question cuz this will eliminate real Jews real quick.

00:02:35.600 --> 00:02:37.200
Does anyone know what Jewish penicillin is?

00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:39.500
Matzo ball soup.

00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:41.500
There it is. She didn't know what it is. Right there.

00:02:41.700 --> 00:02:44.540
It was a little unclear where he was from, and

00:02:44.620 --> 00:02:46.560
why he was telling us like certain things.

00:02:47.060 --> 00:02:48.000
Anyone keep kosher?

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:49.600
I don't, but I don't eat pork.

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:51.960
I mean, kind of? I'm vegan, so like-

00:02:52.860 --> 00:02:56.100
My mom is so proud. She's like "My girl is kosher, and I'm like..."

00:02:56.800 --> 00:02:59.300
I am still stuck on the point that you drove here for this. I am sorry...

00:02:59.300 --> 00:03:00.600
He what?!

00:03:00.600 --> 00:03:02.460
He said he drove here for this.

00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:04.400
I wanted an excuse to come to L.A.

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:07.980
I like took a plane from Seattle.

00:03:08.260 --> 00:03:10.260
You flew here? Yeah. Really? Oh wow.

00:03:10.560 --> 00:03:14.240
I also just like wanted to eat at like, a bunch of vegan places.

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:16.720
Right, we just wanted an excuse to come to L.A.

00:03:16.720 --> 00:03:18.200
I was very comfortable with the girls.

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:21.000
For some reason, the guys gave me a bit of pause.

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:25.400
People always kind of had weird looks cuz I am only half Jewish so growing up, you know

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:27.000
I was in a very, like a Christian environment.

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:30.800
I mean that was the main thing is when we were, you know getting pulled out for the High Holidays.

00:03:30.800 --> 00:03:32.800
Everybody just kind of was just like, 'Why do you get to leave?'

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:34.000
Like stuff like that.

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:35.600
That's the only time it really came up for me.

00:03:59.300 --> 00:03:59.800
Alright!

00:04:01.800 --> 00:04:03.200
Bye!

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:06.400
I have a very Jewish name. I have a very Jewish face.

00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:08.900
Not something that I expected, to be voted out the first time.

00:04:08.900 --> 00:04:11.750
I definitely was expecting to be able to keep playing the rest of the game.

00:04:12.300 --> 00:04:16.200
Adam was my first pick but I wanted to go here just to- just be sure. Okay!

00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:18.560
So tell me why you are Jewish?

00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:23.820
It's harder because you know, I am just Jewish through my mom and there wasn't a big Jewish community where I grew up-

00:04:23.860 --> 00:04:26.300
Actually, like Jewish through your mom rabinically is like full Jewish.

00:04:26.480 --> 00:04:28.020
No, no that's what I mean.

00:04:28.380 --> 00:04:28.880
Just checking.

00:04:28.880 --> 00:04:32.940
No, yes, yeah, of course, so I didn't grow up with a lot of Jewish community around me.

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:37.460
So I didn't do a lot of like the stuff if people grew up in LA or New York or something like that.

00:04:37.460 --> 00:04:39.315
They might have had access to. - Where are you from again?

00:04:39.315 --> 00:04:40.540
Massachusetts, western massachusetts.

00:04:40.760 --> 00:04:45.400
Massachusetts, yes. I didn't really have a religious upbringing at all. And then I did go to college

00:04:45.930 --> 00:04:50.420
at Wesleyan and that is in Connecticut, and it does have a larger Jewish population

00:04:50.420 --> 00:04:52.909
so that's really where I did get to meet a lot of

00:04:53.340 --> 00:04:56.840
Jewish people and really start to experience Jewish culture.

00:04:56.840 --> 00:04:58.760
Who said they didn't do birthright? Did everybody here do birthright?

00:04:59.800 --> 00:05:01.840
I didn't, I didn't- I'm planning to go this winter though.

00:05:03.360 --> 00:05:08.510
I did it in college that was like my- once I went to college it was a much bigger Jewish community.

00:05:08.510 --> 00:05:10.549
So like I got to do stuff like that and I go to birthright, it was awesome.

00:05:10.800 --> 00:05:14.720
I was most suspicious of Garrett because just some of his answers...

00:05:16.620 --> 00:05:19.500
they seemed like very quick and not very detailed.

00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:20.800
Have we all been to Israel?

00:05:20.800 --> 00:05:22.000
Yeah. I was just about to ask that..

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:23.400
So, what's our favorite part of Israel?

00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:25.400
I really loved. Um, I think the Dead Sea was awesome.

00:05:25.580 --> 00:05:30.859
I think Israel is just gorgeous and I was really afraid to go in the Mediterranean Sea because I did not want to get stung

00:05:30.860 --> 00:05:33.600
by jellyfish, so I was like, okay sand.

00:05:33.600 --> 00:05:35.800
I am a beach guy. So, I love the Tel Aviv and Disc Golf Beach.

00:05:36.160 --> 00:05:36.660
What was your favourite part?

00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:40.200
Um, Masada. Going up and like looking down over the Dead Sea and everything.

00:05:40.200 --> 00:05:42.200
What's everyone's favorite dish that their mom makes?

00:05:42.240 --> 00:05:44.960
My grandma's latkes, honestly are like the best thing ever.

00:05:44.960 --> 00:05:46.800
Your favourite food is latkes?

00:05:47.260 --> 00:05:48.400
Have you never had latkes?

00:05:48.400 --> 00:05:50.400
Of course, I had latkes, but it's no one favourite food.

00:05:50.800 --> 00:05:52.400
That's a problem. I don't know, now I'm suspicious.

00:05:52.700 --> 00:05:54.520
You tell me some more about your conversion.

00:05:54.520 --> 00:05:55.400
I was just about to ask that too.

00:05:55.400 --> 00:06:01.779
I grew up like as a kid like going to Hebrew school, having Jewish friends, do a Shabbat every week doing the holidays.

00:06:01.779 --> 00:06:03.939
So it wasn't like, oh my gosh, I'm Jewish now.

00:06:03.939 --> 00:06:05.400
It was just like, okay.

00:06:05.400 --> 00:06:08.800
It's totally fine to convert but just in the name of the game, I was like,

00:06:08.800 --> 00:06:10.800
okay if you converted maybe you're not actually Jewish.

00:06:10.800 --> 00:06:12.400
Maybe someone you know converted.

00:06:12.400 --> 00:06:15.200
Do you feel really in touch with Jewish culture?

00:06:15.220 --> 00:06:18.000
So, I have a lot of Ashkenazi friends who don't buy German cars

00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:19.600
for that very reason like-

00:06:19.600 --> 00:06:22.000
My grandparents won't let me buy or ever get a German car.

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:23.860
Yeah, the Holocaust is probably one of the worst events in history.

00:06:24.139 --> 00:06:27.549
So I don't take for- for anyone to not connect with that. That would be a problem,

00:06:27.550 --> 00:06:30.370
but for me, I would say a lot of Jewish history

00:06:30.370 --> 00:06:35.019
I don't connect with just because it's not part of my history. It doesn't mean that I don't connect to it. Does that make sense?

00:06:35.020 --> 00:06:37.800
Yeah, did you face any discrimination being Filipino and Jewish?

00:06:37.800 --> 00:06:38.770
All the time. Absolutely.

00:06:38.770 --> 00:06:45.660
What about people, like finding us like kind of discriminating in like, a semi-positive way, but not really at all when like when they say-

00:06:46.660 --> 00:06:48.600
Can you smell how much money I'm holding?

00:06:48.600 --> 00:06:51.400
That's terrible. Like I was in an Uber the other day

00:06:51.560 --> 00:06:56.140
and the guy was like, oh you're Jewish. You're powerful. You've got power. You've got connections and I was like, "Alright..."

00:06:57.220 --> 00:06:58.100
You're just you.

00:07:10.400 --> 00:07:11.000
Bye guys. Bye!

00:07:11.150 --> 00:07:15.160
He said his mom was Jewish and if you're born from your mother

00:07:15.160 --> 00:07:20.980
and she's Jewish that makes you a full Jew. So, he just kind of seemed like the one to me from the get-go.

00:07:20.980 --> 00:07:22.600
I kind of saw it was coming.

00:07:22.600 --> 00:07:25.480
I knew it was gonna be a little bit harder. People who are Jewish are very

00:07:25.480 --> 00:07:29.079
you know, practicing in their culture and to you know,

00:07:29.080 --> 00:07:35.260
have all the little details down and things like that is definitely hard for somebody who didn't you know, grow up practicing Judaism.

00:07:45.470 --> 00:07:50.589
After Garrett got voted out. I was kind of actually weary about Arielle.

00:07:50.700 --> 00:07:56.679
I want to hear more about your because I mean, there are Israelis that- that aren't Jewish and like that. Yes, that's cool, too

00:07:56.679 --> 00:07:58.679
I was just gonna ask that about you.

00:07:58.679 --> 00:08:00.110
I know. I am definitely like-

00:08:00.110 --> 00:08:05.169
I was thinking about this whole time I was like, oh my god, but like are you practicing or...

00:08:05.169 --> 00:08:08.859
No, So I- I do I went to Hebrew school. I went to the JCC at first grade.

00:08:08.860 --> 00:08:11.720
I- I switched to a private school, IV Academia.

00:08:11.720 --> 00:08:12.840
Can we speak right now?

00:08:17.000 --> 00:08:19.810
I was getting scared people were gonna start voting for me because I was

00:08:20.270 --> 00:08:24.430
definitely putting out more Israeli than Jewish and that is kind of my identity.

00:08:24.430 --> 00:08:27.820
Like, I definitely fall into that more because I am a secular Jew.

00:08:27.820 --> 00:08:32.919
I'm black, Chinese and Filipino, and for most places I go. Well, some people just don't even know what I am in general.

00:08:33.610 --> 00:08:36.400
Add Jewish into mix and that really throws people off.

00:08:36.400 --> 00:08:38.810
You said you were born here- born and raised in LA

00:08:39.310 --> 00:08:40.940
Yeah, but I went to school in a very

00:08:40.940 --> 00:08:46.960
conservative state and now I'm back because it was really hard and part of the reason it was so hard was because I am Jewish

00:08:46.960 --> 00:08:48.730
and I did not feel accepted. Yes,

00:08:48.730 --> 00:08:51.159
there were a lot of people who did accept me, but you know

00:08:51.160 --> 00:08:54.780
sometimes a little bit of hate can overrule a lot of love.

00:08:54.780 --> 00:08:56.110
And you said you went from a Jewish high school?

00:08:56.210 --> 00:08:59.200
Yeah, Jewish elementary school, Jewish preschool, Jewish high school.

00:08:59.200 --> 00:09:00.920
She was just so outgoing and

00:09:00.920 --> 00:09:05.100
talking about her experience of going to an out-of-state school

00:09:05.300 --> 00:09:08.890
and that wasn't Jewish and since she'd went through a Jewish school her whole life,

00:09:08.890 --> 00:09:12.999
I think that was one of the big things that kind of went off in my head that maybe it was her.

00:09:13.000 --> 00:09:16.450
You know, how do you go from a Jewish school your whole life and not go to a Jewish college?

00:09:16.450 --> 00:09:19.659
I was on a dating app recently. There was a guy who sent me a photo of

00:09:20.269 --> 00:09:25.599
himself, bottoms on but he was shirtless because he was like really buff and he like wanted to show it off, I didn't care.

00:09:26.300 --> 00:09:32.259
And he had like a lot of tattoos and I was like looking at it and he had a giant swastika right here.

00:09:32.800 --> 00:09:36.368
And I messaged him back. I said "Am I being pranked?" Like-

00:09:37.399 --> 00:09:41.469
Like and I said, why do you have a swastika on your arm? He said it's a Chinese

00:09:41.470 --> 00:09:45.600
peace symbol and I said, oh honey. Oh, honey. No like not anymore

00:09:46.129 --> 00:09:52.178
My first day at Calabasas High there were swastikas all over the school. My sophomore year,

00:09:52.179 --> 00:09:57.309
this kid came up to me he's like "I hate Jews like, I am a full anti-Semite.

00:09:57.309 --> 00:10:02.889
I hate you and your people" and I'm like "Dude, I don't know you like we're just in a class together.

00:10:02.929 --> 00:10:07.119
Why are you at this school if you hate Jews? Go move somewhere else." - And also he doesn't even know you.

00:10:07.239 --> 00:10:10.959
I've been told you know, you and your family you should have died in the Holocaust.

00:10:11.480 --> 00:10:13.480
You and your people are evil.

00:10:14.379 --> 00:10:19.479
You don't deserve a place here. Things like that and it hurts, but at the end of the day

00:10:19.480 --> 00:10:21.980
I feel also like it made me stronger.

00:10:21.980 --> 00:10:24.080
That reminds me. How do you guys feel about tattoos?

00:10:24.080 --> 00:10:27.960
Oh, I have a tattoo. I have got a few. Yeah. Yeah. I don't have any. I won't get any.

00:10:29.640 --> 00:10:33.460
I think Israelis love tattoos. Tel Aviv is the most tatted up place.

00:10:33.460 --> 00:10:34.540
Yeah, Yeah. True.

00:10:34.540 --> 00:10:36.300
Jerusalem likes to hate it

00:10:53.220 --> 00:10:55.220
Sorry! You just know so much.

00:10:56.100 --> 00:10:58.200
I know so much. You know so much.

00:10:58.300 --> 00:11:00.400
No, you know so much. Okay!

00:11:12.000 --> 00:11:15.200
Oh my god, you guys! I am feeling good.

00:11:15.600 --> 00:11:17.000
If those lights turn red.

00:11:19.400 --> 00:11:19.900
Yes!

00:11:21.800 --> 00:11:22.800
We are the best.

00:11:22.900 --> 00:11:24.200
I am so excited.

00:11:24.200 --> 00:11:25.200
Oh my god!

00:11:29.800 --> 00:11:31.500
Oh, knew it!

00:11:31.500 --> 00:11:32.100
Yes!

00:11:33.640 --> 00:11:38.360
I just live with somebody who's Jewish and have been in the culture now for like a year and a half

00:11:38.360 --> 00:11:40.100
A groupie at college?

00:11:40.100 --> 00:11:41.919
Yes, because he was sitting right next to me.

00:11:41.919 --> 00:11:48.069
He was really quiet so I can tell when people were asking questions that he wasn't stepping in to answer them

00:11:48.069 --> 00:11:52.140
Yeah, so as the mole I came in actually taking stories from people who are Jewish

00:11:52.660 --> 00:11:57.240
and kind of co-opting them as my own because I had to have a lot of Jewish friends.

00:11:57.249 --> 00:12:00.780
So, I have experienced the culture through them. I'm just happy I made it past the first round.

00:12:00.789 --> 00:12:04.029
I was surprised that they voted Adam out real- really quick. It just shows that

00:12:05.119 --> 00:12:10.329
you can't tell who somebody is just by looking at them. You really have to get to know them a little- a little better.

00:12:13.800 --> 00:12:16.200
Yeah! I don't wanna play into the stereotypes.

00:12:16.800 --> 00:12:17.300
I am cool with it.

00:12:17.300 --> 00:12:20.100
You know, we are gonna be in like a strip club right now.

00:12:20.100 --> 00:12:22.100
Let's go! Let's go!

00:12:23.900 --> 00:12:28.190
I'm a Jewish atheist, which if it came up it might have been something that

00:12:28.770 --> 00:12:33.379
would have gotten me in trouble more so but it's your culture. It's your everything.

00:12:33.810 --> 00:12:36.859
It's a big identity and we need to hold onto it because

00:12:37.380 --> 00:12:41.400
If we don't, people will try to make us do it by force.

00:12:41.400 --> 00:12:42.660
Within the Jewish community,

00:12:42.660 --> 00:12:45.400
There's probably more stereotypes than outside of the Jewish community.

00:12:45.400 --> 00:12:46.320
By that I mean,

00:12:46.320 --> 00:12:50.680
there's a lot of judgment within some of the communities whether you're more Jewish than someone or less Jewish than someone.

00:12:50.680 --> 00:12:54.380
You came from Israel, You came from Russia, You came from Germany, You came to the States.

00:12:54.380 --> 00:12:55.700
I don't make it the full thing

00:12:55.700 --> 00:12:59.720
but it's very much a part of me and my values and the way I live my life and you know,

00:12:59.720 --> 00:13:01.400
there are not that many Jews in the world

00:13:01.400 --> 00:13:08.599
and so to be part of such a small but very close group is actually really rewarding in a lot of ways and

00:13:09.060 --> 00:13:11.640
I'm very happy with being Jewish and I love it.

00:13:12.140 --> 00:13:15.100
When did like everybody become a Democrat?

00:13:15.100 --> 00:13:17.980
Honestly, when I was at school, I grew up in a really small town in

00:13:17.990 --> 00:13:22.380
Nebraska. It was very white. We had Fox News on TV. All the time.

00:13:22.380 --> 00:13:24.380
- You're not helping your case. - I know..am not helping.  - I know my vote.

00:13:24.660 --> 00:13:30.400
I am a Democrat.

00:13:30.930 --> 00:13:32.930
One of them is a liar.

